{
  "version": 1,
  "provenance": {
    "bounds": "The two world-level offsets contain 14 meaningful native bytes each and end at independently referenced next arrays. The world event array contains 14 nonzero or 0xFF entries followed by two zero alignment bytes, which are not owned here. The random world selector explicitly uses modulo 13; both 13-byte world selectors retain their independent physical bases and leave their one-byte zero tails outside their object extents. Fourteen actual world-text pointers end at the level-offset table. The native map-generation dispatch contains 14 distinct boolean callbacks; the script interpreter has exactly two command handlers. The map-check dispatcher has 10 callback slots and ends at its existing TaskDesc name. Native function targets and all regional literal references are checked separately.",
    "types": "The map-generation callbacks return only 0 or 1 and have no direct source callers. Their definitions use u8, matching the established u8 function-pointer table and eliminating incompatible callback types. Existing body bytes and relocations must remain unchanged. World names use the established version-native MapNameText rather than integer addresses."
  },
